    Dogfood walk 2026-11-04 at tip d02916e: the three README Quick start commands run
    with env -i and a fresh empty HOME, CRIER_URL and BUNKER_SERVER unset.
    README.md:32-34 says "all three commands reach their checkers and fail with the
    missing value named". Measured — step 1 aborts at bunker-server-install.sh:14
    (${BUNKER_SERVER:?}) and step 3 aborts at node-create.sh:70 (${SERVER:?}); both
    print the script's own line number, print no PASS/FAIL row, and never reach a
    checker. Only step 2 reaches its ladder (nine PASS rows, four named FAIL rows,
    NODE: FAIL (4)).
    
    The sentence has no command attached, so nothing in tests/selftest.sh can
    contradict it — the same claim-without-a-probe class as CF-081. CF-009 and CF-041
    are complete on their own criteria and are not re-opened: CF-009 AC2 asked that
    the export be documented before the command (README.md:17-20 now does) and CF-041
    AC2 asked for a flag project-node.sh accepts (step 2 now uses one). What no row
    owns is this promise.
    
    The node leg was also walked again on a reachable host: node-create spawned,
    staged (now including reclaim_disk.py from 27df6ac), provisioned, and reported the
    same honest FAIL set (crier_url, harness apply, crier_identity), then cloned at
    layer 40 after the bus layer had failed. --ttl 1h measured as exactly one hour on
    the created agent, which no earlier walk had recorded; the agent was destroyed
    afterwards and the host was back to its pre-existing single agent. Reproductions
    recorded, not re-filed: CF-126 (CRIER_URL never forwarded), CF-127 (/tmp pip log),
    CF-080 (clone after a failed bus layer), CF-072 (-> 000000), CF-087 (staged-set
    matcher spelling and scope, re-run hermetically), all still live at this tip.
    
    Evidence: docs/audits/code-factory-dogfood-2026-11-04-02-20-15.md, which carries
    every captured block verbatim. Board ids were renumbered by the append helper
    (delta=1) after a sibling lane consumed the drafted CF-144 at 51efb66.
    
    Gates at this tree: bash scripts/boardctl validate RESULT: OK (50 warnings,
    board canon; the probe-key warnings are this board's established shape);
    bash tests/selftest.sh SELFTEST: PASS. gh run list returns [] — this repo ships
    no workflows, so the selftest is the CI-equivalent gate.
    
    Guard note: board-and-docs-only diff, so Tier 1 reports lint=no staged files and
    refuses it; committed with core.hooksPath=/dev/null per the repository's disclosed
